Hello, here is the latest account newsletter from Northstar Domains.

A quick note on the shipping labels: the new format puts the order reference =
above the address block. Older labels are still accepted, but please switch w=
hen you next reprint a batch.

The holiday rota for our support desk is confirmed. There will always be some=
one on duty during working hours, though replies may take a little longer in =
the busiest week.

Thanks again for the update on the spring order. The warehouse confirmed that=
 the pallets arrived in good condition and the count matched the packing list=
, so nothing further is needed on our side for that delivery.

Some customers have asked whether the outer cartons can be recycled. They can=
, and from next month the cartons will carry a small printed note saying so o=
n the side panel.

The assembly guides are now available in larger print. They were redesigned a=
fter feedback from a care home that orders from us, and the new layout is eas=
ier for everyone to read.

The new storage racks in our main warehouse are now in use. They give us room=
 for about a fifth more stock, which should shorten the wait on the items tha=
t sold out last winter.

The office move on our side is finished. Phone extensions and team names are =
the same, so you should not notice any difference when you contact the usual =
people.

The revised care instructions are now printed inside each box lid. The wordin=
g is shorter and easier to follow, and the diagrams match the current version=
 of the product.

We have extended the warranty on the heavier units from one year to two. Noth=
ing changes in how claims are handled; the longer period simply applies to or=
ders from this month.

Thank you for being a Northstar customer.

--=20
